<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  ClickHouse server override mounted into /etc/clickhouse-server/config.d/, by
  the compose `clickhouse` service and by
  .github/workflows/scripts/start-clickhouse.sh alike, so a lane that runs out
  of memory in CI runs out of memory the same way on a laptop.

  What actually bounds the server is its container's cgroup limit
  (CLICKHOUSE_MEM_LIMIT): ClickHouse reads it and sizes both its memory cap and
  its caches from that. This file only moves the cap further under it, which is
  why it holds a ratio and no absolute size — the limit differs per caller.

  INVARIANT: this ratio must leave room for what the server does not track.
  Allocator overhead and mmap'd mark files sit outside its accounting, so at the
  0.9 default a container can reach its cgroup limit while ClickHouse still
  believes it is within budget — and then the kernel kills the server rather
  than ClickHouse rejecting one query with MEMORY_LIMIT_EXCEEDED. A killed
  server surfaces as a connection error in whichever test was running.
-->
<clickhouse>
  <max_server_memory_usage_to_ram_ratio>0.8</max_server_memory_usage_to_ram_ratio>
</clickhouse>
